KZ3 patch 2053 (RSX pass 55): device-local vertex and index rings (opt-in: LD_VB_DEVICE=1; default off).

The walker writes vertices and indices into UPLOAD-heap rings and the GPU read them from system memory over
PCIe. Patch 2052's timestamps showed the main pass's 700 position-only depth draws of one PSO costing 16 ms of
GPU per frame. Each draw now reads from a DEFAULT-heap mirror of the ring (same offsets, per frame slot,
LD_VB_DEVICE_MB = 128 MB vertex / a quarter of that index) and every submit first executes a small copy list
that copies the byte range the list's draws used. Draws whose range does not fit the mirror keep reading the
upload ring. Mirrors rest in COMMON between lists (copy list: COMMON -> COPY_DEST -> COMMON).
Measured in pass 55 (K4 level): draw GPU time 65 -> 35 ms/frame but the copy lists cost 22-25 ms/frame
(50 MB/frame at ~2 GB/s on a GPU the driver keeps at P5/P8 with PCIe gen 1-2), so no net gain: default off.
